.TH TMPNAM_R 3
.SH NAME
tmpnam_r \- reentrant generation of a temporary filename
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library
.RI ( libc ", " \-lc )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "char *tmpnam_r(char *" s ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmpnam_r
is the reentrant equivalent of
.BR tmpnam (3).
It writes a candidate temporary-file pathname into the caller-supplied buffer
.IR s ,
which must hold at least
.B L_tmpnam
bytes, and returns
.IR s .
Unlike
.BR tmpnam (3),
passing NULL does not fall back to a shared static buffer.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.IR s ,
or NULL if
.I s
is NULL.
.SH NOTES
As with
.BR tmpnam (3),
there is a race between choosing the name and creating the file; prefer
.BR mkstemp (3)
or
.BR tmpfile (3)
in new code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmpnam (3),
.BR mkstemp (3),
.BR tmpfile (3)
.SH STANDARDS
GNU extension.
